{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1530244-how-different-is-wod-mortal-to-cofd-mortal","id":1530244,"title":"How different is WoD mortal to CofD mortal?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-07T21:36:32-08:00","id":1530244,"title":"How different is WoD mortal to CofD mortal?","content":"I feel that they're different, but I can't really tell what the difference are?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T00:34:19-08:00","id":1530250,"title":"","content":"There's a bunch:<br /> <br /> 1) Support. Plain and simple, there's just a lot more books for mortals in the CofD. CofD mortals (esp. in 1e comparatively) felt like an actual game-line, not an afterthought in the rules. The WoD didn't actually have a &quot;normal mortal&quot; creation rules in a book until Revised (WoD: Mafia), as every other book that had rules presumed some supernatural involvement (even if just being hunters).<br /> <br /> 2) How the supernatural is hidden. In the WoD the supernatural is hidden from mortals by overt conspiracies run by the supernaturals. This means mortals have to be shoved down on the ladder so they can be subjected to such efforts successfully. Even the theoretical advantage humans have in ingenuity and numbers really never matters in the face of huge powerful supernatural bodies like the Camarilla and the Technocracy keeping humanity in the dark. In the CofD humanity disbelieves as a coping mechanism. Humans self-select for those that ignore the supernatural elements of their world because it's safer than confronting those things. Supernaturals don't need global conspiracies to keep themselves safe because it's OK for humans to think things exist on some level as long as nobody is blabbing important details. <br /> <br /> 3) Mortals are the baseline of CofD. In the WoD, supernaturals are the baseline. Characters are created by making them according to the rules of their supernatural type. In the CofD, you start with a mortal character and layer the supernatural on top of it. This means most games can even start as mortals before they become supernaturals (though not all), and every game forefronts that all PCs have connections to mortal lives (even stolen ones for Demons). <br /> <br /> So, basically, the CofD makes mortals matter more. Not that mortals are powerful or can take on the supernatural with ease compared to the WoD, but they have more narrative weight, and more of a presence to carry their own stories within the dangers of the dark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T05:21:39-08:00","id":1530266,"title":"","content":"Does WoD Mortal handle Supernatural better than CofD mortal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T07:53:14-08:00","id":1530274,"title":"","content":"To me, the CofD mortal has more general weirdness going on I've heard it said that every mortal in Chronicles has had some interaction with the supernatural in some point in their lifetime, wether or not they realize it, and that rings true. That doesn't mean just an encounter with a splat, it could have been an encounter with a spirit, or maybe a piece of messed up infrastructure makes everyone walk backwards in an area but makes them not realize they're walking backwards, or maybe they find a relic or something. The Supernatural in CofD is, IMO, more fantastical than in WoD. <br /> <br /> In WoD, you may have mortals that go their whole lives without encountering the supernatural directly, but they are being plotted against by the supernatural. Things are being put into their food to make them more irritable to increase domestic violence rates, politicians are being bribed to loosen regulations for pollutions and even those loosened regulations are being skirted around, etc. The supernatural in WoD is more actively antagonistic towards humanity than in CofD. <br /> <br /> Which isn't at all to mean that there aren't antagonistic factions in CofD, the Exarchs absolutely are, and the God Machine can be, but it's still more about achieving their goals than it is about getting parents to abuse their children. <br /> <br /> Now to which &quot;world&quot; has people handle the supernatural better? Realistically? Neither of them. They're both built with the idea that mortals don't know the supernatural exists and in both a frenzied vampire or a frenzied / kuruth wereworlf leads to a dead mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T08:44:36-08:00","id":1530277,"title":"","content":"I feel like Mortal was more important in WoD than in CofD? Like even through CofD mortal are more important narritive wise, they aren't really that important in the grand scheme of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T12:25:32-08:00","id":1530306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1530244-how-different-is-wod-mortal-to-cofd-mortal?p=1530277#post1530277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like Mortal was more important in WoD than in CofD? Like even through CofD mortal are more important narritive wise, they aren't really that important in the grand scheme of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the focus of the individual game you're running. But a mortal-run conspiracy is one of the prominent possible explanations for VII in Requiem, one of the five Forsaken Tribes considers man to be the greatest concern and the most important prey to focus on, Promethean is a game all about learning about mortal life and aspiring to one day understand and achieve it as a celebration, Hunter features <i>numerous</i> worldwide mortal conspiracies including the US government's black budget monster containment division and the descendants of the mystic order that once was equaled by the order that figures into the origin of Clan Mekhet, and Deviant <i>also</i> features numerous worldwide mortal conspiracies and centers around mortal conspiracies as both the primary antagonist and the typical party responsible for the Divergence of the titular deviants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T12:26:01-08:00","id":1530308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1530244-how-different-is-wod-mortal-to-cofd-mortal?p=1530266#post1530266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does WoD Mortal handle Supernatural better than CofD mortal?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I understand your question, keeping in mind that &quot;Supernatural&quot; is a TV show about two monster hunting brothers, so there could be confusion about if you're asking about which game-line to run a Supernatural show style game in, or you mean something else with Supernatural.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1530244-how-different-is-wod-mortal-to-cofd-mortal?p=1530277#post1530277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like Mortal was more important in WoD than in CofD? Like even through CofD mortal are more important narritive wise, they aren't really that important in the grand scheme of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that humanity as a whole is more important in the WoD, where individual mortals are more important in the CofD; hence CofD is usually better for actually player mortals. One mortal in the WoD really doesn't meant anything, thus telling a story about them as the main character is difficult; too much is simply beyond their reach to interact with in a meaningful way. One mortal in the CofD can matter more because there's a lot more low stakes things happening in the CofD. There's no looming End Times or grand Masquerade far beyond them. Werewolves and mages might be far better suited at dealing with a problematic spirit in either, but in the CofD mortals can solve the problems a spirit is causing where in the WoD they're basically locked out of doing anything with agency about it (or have to join a hunter group that can get them low level supernatural stuff to get over that entry bar).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T18:11:15-08:00","id":1530331,"title":"","content":"Humanity in WoD seem to have shard of the Divine, can turn into Mage, seem to be needed for the World to continue to exist, they can create Banality, have the Concensus, can be Imbue, and is part of God plan.<br /> While in CofD human aren't that important, the God Machine probably have other planet it's can built infrastructure on, The Supernal realm and Mage will still continue to exist without Humanity, Vampire, Beast, Changeling, Demon, and Promethean need humanity, but because they humanity to feed and hide from their problem, not because humanity is special, Mummy, and Geist doesn't really need humanity, since Geist can just eat Other Ghost and Spirit if they powerful enough, Deviant wouldn't exist without humanity, which is probably for the best, and Werewolf isn't human, but without humanity, they got no mate, at least for the forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T20:02:24-08:00","id":1530337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1530244-how-different-is-wod-mortal-to-cofd-mortal?p=1530331#post1530331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humanity in WoD seem to have shard of the Divine, can turn into Mage, seem to be needed for the World to continue to exist, they can create Banality, have the Concensus, can be Imbue, and is part of God plan.<br /> While in CofD human aren't that important, the God Machine probably have other planet it's can built infrastructure on, The Supernal realm and Mage will still continue to exist without Humanity, Vampire, Beast, Changeling, Demon, and Promethean need humanity, but because they humanity to feed and hide from their problem, not because humanity is special, Mummy, and Geist doesn't really need humanity, since Geist can just eat Other Ghost and Spirit if they powerful enough, Deviant wouldn't exist without humanity, which is probably for the best, and Werewolf isn't human, but without humanity, they got no mate, at least for the forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummies harvest relics created by humans, steer human culture, are most often summoned by their human cults, and have as part of their creation mythology the notion that humans were created as sacrifices to keep the force of entropy from ending the universe.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine's theoretical capacity to pull up stakes and start over elsewhere in the universe notwithstanding, the vast majority of its endeavors involve processes currently only used with any commonality among human society to such a degree that it is one of the forces in Chronicles actively working to keep things from getting better. Humanity is where it keeps a bunch of its stuff.<br /> <br /> I could go into the rest, but suffice it to say it's not clear what you're getting at here besides a very abstract hypothetical of &quot;which supernaturals could survive if the rest of humanity disappeared?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T01:01:06-08:00","id":1530348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1530244-how-different-is-wod-mortal-to-cofd-mortal?p=1530331#post1530331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humanity in WoD seem to have shard of the Divine, can turn into Mage, seem to be needed for the World to continue to exist, they can create Banality, have the Concensus, can be Imbue, and is part of God plan.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not untrue that Chronicles of Darkness takes a less cosmically anthropocentric view of the world. WoD has an explicit Christian God and other divine figures that take personal interest in the destiny of mankind. Chronicles of Darkness tends towards a view that no one is particularly in the driver's seat, and to the degree that some forces are, they are impersonal and distant. The universe is where humanity exists, but it does not exist for humanity's sake. Humanity is adrift and each person must find the meaning in their life themselves.<br /> <br /> That's not the same as Chronicles of Darkness not finding meaning and importance in human lives. A number of Chronicles games have a powerful humanist streak running through them, the attitude that while the universe may not issue humanity an intrinsic meaning to exist, human lives are still filled with self-created meaning, beauty and value. A number of the supernatural splats are typified by yearning for or admiring these qualities: Prometheans, many Changelings and some Demons see something valuable and enviable in an ordinary human life.<br /> <br /> If your life doesn't shift the world, your living doesn't change history or alter the course of wars or nations, does that mean your life was not important?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1530244-how-different-is-wod-mortal-to-cofd-mortal?p=1530331#post1530331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire, Beast, Changeling, Demon, and Promethean need humanity, but because they humanity to feed and hide from their problem, not because humanity is special</div> </div> </div> </div>Promethean definitely, explicitly cares about humanity because humanity is special. Perhaps not in a cosmic sense, but the entire game is about the Pilgrimage to seek the achievement of mortality and the moments of growth where the Created bond with others and see what they prize about a mortal life. The Pilgrimage is about becoming mortal, and without it, the Created are lost to misery. The lack of a mortal human life <i>is</i> the problem they flee from.<br /> <br /> Most changeling societies do not use humanity simply to farm glamour and hide from the Hunt. Changeling is all about reclaiming your life or forging a new life after recovering from the Durance, and for many changelings, that means a life among mortal humans, in the community they were torn away from. It's a rare and cynical changeling that views the mortal crowds as glamour jars and hiding places.<br /> <br /> Even Beasts, who define themselves in opposition to mortal humanity, feed off of humanity because of that opposition. They are elemental monsters, the lurking darkness, empowered by a connection to the seam between the world-soul and the collective soul of humanity. Without eyes to see the darkness and fear what is imagined within, the lurking darkness would have no power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T02:42:38-08:00","id":1530354,"title":"","content":"What about Psychology then? Is there any difference there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-13T08:11:07-08:00","id":1530743,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s Integrity instead of Morality which makes an impact if that\u2019s what you mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T17:55:08-08:00","id":1531154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1530244-how-different-is-wod-mortal-to-cofd-mortal#post1530244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that they're different, but I can't really tell what the difference are?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a comparison of OWoD, really.<br /> <br /> CoD is basically designed around mortals. In OWoD, mortals were an after-thought; the main game was Vampire: the Masquerade. In OWoD, &quot;You want to play a what now? But, they're so weak&quot;. CoD/NWoD, has entire game-systems, for mortals. like Immortals, Second-Sight etc. Mortals in OWoD only get a few pages in V:tPG and if you get Hunter's Hunted, that's even better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}